0803/: project 0803 (incunabula) in the stand-in layout the VRE bridge writes: the Ready token
0803/.ready, and the generation it names, 0803/20261007T000000Z-00000000/, holding snapshot.nq, the
interim-DAO snapshot sync-store serves. The fixture is a test input and, until access-server's image
stops carrying it, the data the image serves; in a deployment with the VRE bridge, the bridge's output
replaces it.

The token is hand-written: generation 20261007T000000Z-00000000 and as_of 2026-10-07T00:00:00Z (the
dump's bagging date below), server prod, interim format version 1, transformation version 1, no
previous generation, and the inputs digest of 0803's shipped inputs as the VRE bridge computes it
(areas/deposit/vre-bridge/inputs/0803/, pinned by that bridge's refresh_0803 test; no reader checks it).
media/data/0803/.ready holds the same bytes, so the two tokens hold equal provenance.

snapshot.nq is the file that was 0803.nq here, moved with its bytes unchanged. It is dao-lift's output,
not the VRE bridge's: it lacks the dao:accessRights and dao:dataClassification lines interim format
version 1 has, and any dao:valueHasXml line (sync-store reads none of them). Its token names format
version 1 nonetheless, since sync-store reads nothing it lacks. The fixture's Ready tokens keep
transformation version 1, that of the lift that produced snapshot.nq.

