  produced by:     dsp vre project dump -s prod -p 0803 --skip-assets --cleanup

The stage dump this file was first built from (api.stage.dasch.swiss, bagged 2026-07-19, DSP-API v37.1.0)
gave the same bytes.

Producer
  dao-lift:        dasch-swiss/dsp-incubator@b2226ff4a987bf5f4b5cd0f33a8bf923a3033c7f
                   (cpe/tools/dao-lift)

That commit's cpe/tools/dao-lift/FORMAT.md is the format the file follows; interim format version 1,
areas/deposit/vre-bridge/lift/FORMAT.md, adds the rights and classification lines and
dao:valueHasXml to it.

Regenerate from the incubator's cpe/ directory, at the commit above, on the unzipped dump:

  cargo run --locked --release --manifest-path tools/dao-lift/Cargo.toml -- snapshot <dump-dir> <out.nq>

The output is byte-identical for the same dump. A regenerated file keeps sync-store's committed-file
tests green without changing their expectations: those come from the dump. Every row of
areas/access/media/data/0803/20261007T000000Z-00000000/curation.csv names a resource of this file.
If a regenerated file drops one, CPE leaves Incunabula not ready until the row is removed or re-keyed
by hand.

0803-arks.txt: the 0803 data ARKs Incunabula stores, which are dao-lift's output. One plain data ARK
per line, sorted, 4,143 lines.

Source
  file:            cpe/projects/incunabula/data.sql (the resources.ark and annotations.ark columns)
  repository:      dasch-swiss/dsp-incubator, at commit c2b3e10a8d7c695347e11ed7a5cf31bf0f3dca64

Extract it in the incubator checkout at that commit:

  grep -oE 'https://ark\.dasch\.swiss/ark:/72163/1/0803/[A-Za-z0-9_=]+' cpe/projects/incunabula/data.sql | LC_ALL=C sort -u

It is a subset of the served resources: no LinkObj, 64 of 77 Regions, no calibration-scan Pages. The
committed tests check each line against the served ARK. Like snapshot.nq, it is a frozen copy and does not
follow the incubator.
